{# The button skin as a bare class string, so the <button> in the contact form
   and the <a> in the header wear the same clothes without either copy
   drifting from the other. The contrast rule lives here and nowhere else:
   accent fill with a white label, and a hover that DARKENS — the purple is a
   dark brand, so lightening would drop the label below AA.

   The secondary tone is the fact chip of the hero grown to button size:
   white on a hairline, the same shape and the same measurements. It exists so
   two calls to action can stand side by side without competing — one filled,
   one outlined. Its label is neutral-900 on white (17.4:1), its hairline
   darkens on hover rather than lightening.

   Emits no markup. Pull it with include(), assign it, hand it to `class`.
   Params: size ('default' or 'compact') and tone ('primary' or 'secondary').
   Compact is the header, where the bar is 80 pixels high and the button
   shares the row with the burger; it holds 44 pixels so a thumb still finds
   it on a phone. #}
{%- set size = size|default('default') -%}
{%- set tone = tone|default('primary') -%}
{%- set skin = tone == 'secondary'
    ? 'border border-neutral-200 bg-white text-neutral-900 hover:border-neutral-300 hover:bg-neutral-50'
    : 'bg-accent text-white hover:bg-accent-hover' -%}
{%- set base = 'inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-lg font-mono font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.15em] transition-colors ' ~ skin -%}
{%- set measures = size == 'compact'
    ? 'h-11 px-4 text-xs sm:px-5'
    : 'px-6 py-3.5 text-sm' -%}
{{- base ~ ' ' ~ measures -}}
